---

<section id="work" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#fafafa] dark:bg-[var(--c-page)] text-dark dark:text-[var(--c-ink)] px-8 md:px-16 py-24 md:py-32 transition-colors duration-500">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto relative z-10">
    <!-- Kicker -->
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.24em] opacity-50 mb-6">
      <span class="text-sunset">—</span> 01 · Selected work
    </p>

    <!-- Heading -->
    <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-[1.02] tracking-[-0.01em] mb-6">
      Selected work.
    </h2>

    <!-- Lead -->
    <p class="font-serif italic text-xl md:text-2xl leading-snug max-w-3xl mb-14 opacity-90">
      Essays in editing, two analyses built on data and code, and four demos —
      agent, OCR, mail, reports — linked below.
    </p>

    <!-- Divider -->
    <hr class="border-t border-dark/10 dark:border-[var(--c-line)] w-full mb-14" />

    <!-- Highlighted cards: analyses (essays card skipped — no EN articles yet) -->
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
      <a
        href="/en/articles/what-the-data-says-ai-adoption-poland-vs-eu/"
        class="group rounded-lg border border-dark/15 bg-dark text-primary p-7 hover:border-accent transition-colors duration-200 no-underline block"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-[#e1f3fe]"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#8fb9d4]">Data analysis · GUS × Eurostat</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mb-2 leading-snug">AI Adoption: Poland vs EU</h3>
        <p class="font-sans text-sm opacity-80 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Hand-written SQL reconciles the same indicator between GUS and Eurostat:
          Poland adopts fast, but from a low base, so the EU gap grows. With figures, sources, dates — plus a downloadable report.
        </p>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent group-hover:underline">
          analysis + report (PDF) ↗
        </span>
      </a>
      <a
        href="/en/articles/bm25-vs-embeddings-a-retrieval-benchmark/"
        class="group rounded-lg border border-dark/15 bg-dark text-primary p-7 hover:border-accent transition-colors duration-200 no-underline block"
      >
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
          <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 bg-[#fdebec]"></span>
          <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-[#c98a88]">Experiment · benchmark</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-serif text-xl mb-2 leading-snug">BM25 versus embeddings</h3>
        <p class="font-sans text-sm opacity-80 leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Does semantics always win over words? A purpose-built bench
          shows plainly that it does not — and at which point search
          by meaning breaks down.
        </p>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent group-hover:underline">
          read the analysis ↗
        </span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Live: infrastructure -->
    <div class="mb-14 border border-dark/15 rounded-lg p-5 bg-white">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] opacity-55 mb-3">On the wire</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-2 font-sans text-sm">
        <p><a href="https://demo.mjoldak.pl" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-semibold underline decoration-1 underline-offset-4 hover:opacity-70">Sales Agent B2B</a> —
          <span class="opacity-70">form → GenAI lead classification, EU-hosted database, human in the loop</span></p>
        <p><span class="font-semibold">n8n Pipeline (MCP)</span> —
          <span class="opacity-70">Webhook → Gemini → EU database, callable by agents as a tool</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Open source — 10 repos -->
